course: dictionary
lesson: 8485
title: Sandbanks
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A sandbank is a raised area of sand in a river, at the coast or in the sea. At high tide it may be hidden under the water, so you might not see it at all. «Know the tide times; the rising sea can cut you off on rocks, sandbanks or around cliffs.»
explain: Sandbanks form where moving water drops the sand it carries. This is called deposition. The water slows down, the sand settles, and over time a bank builds up in rivers, estuaries and along coasts.
explain: Sandbanks can be dangerous. A boat can run aground on one, which means it gets stuck on the sand. People walking out to a sandbank can be cut off, because «on a flat beach the tide can come back in faster than you can walk».
fact: A sandbank is a raised area of sand in a river, at the coast or in the sea.
fact: Some sandbanks are hidden under the water when the tide is high.
fact: Sandbanks form by deposition, when moving water drops the sand it carries.
fact: Seals often rest on sandbanks.
fact: To run aground means to get stuck on the bottom, such as on a sandbank.
exercise: What is a sandbank? | *A raised area of sand in a river, at the coast or in the sea | A kind of sea bird | A steep cliff made of rock | A deep hole dug in the seabed
exercise: «The rising sea can cut you off on sandbanks.» What does cut you off mean here? | Carry you out to a boat | *Trap you so you cannot get back to land | Wash you clean with a wave | Stop you from swimming
exercise: Sandbanks form when moving water drops the sand it carries. What is this process called? | Evaporation | Erosion | *Deposition
test: Why might a boat run aground on a sandbank? | Because the sea is too calm | Because it is full of fish | *Because it gets stuck on the sand | Because it has no engine
test: Why is it dangerous to walk out to a sandbank on a flat beach? | It hides under the water at low tide | Seals might bite you | The sand is too soft to stand on | *The tide can come back in faster than you can walk
exam: Which statement is true? | Sandbanks are made of rock | A sandbank is always above the water | *Seals often rest on sandbanks | Sandbanks are only found in deserts
